The equivalence $\Phi$ has the natural localization and coefficient compatibilities $$\label{eq:G5}
 \begin{gathered}
 \begin{tikzcd}[ampersand replacement=\&,column sep=large,row sep=large]
 \mathcal C \arrow[r,"L"] \arrow[dr,"e_B(S')^\vee"']
   \& A \arrow[d,"\Phi"] \\
   \& B
 \end{tikzcd}
 \\[1ex]
 R\simeq(M')^\vee e_B^{-1}\Phi.
 \end{gathered}$$ They hold with the full Ran family structures: they commute with collisions, insertion of vacua, disjoint products, and the base operations in the local comparison and period construction. The first compatibility uniquely determines $\Phi$, with its specified comparison, on the localization quotient.

